1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Nineties Hollywood Icons — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,964
Welcome to Nineties Hollywood Icons, Then and Now.

3
00:00:15,064 --> 00:00:21,092
Winona Ryder made offbeat characters feel instantly
memorable in Beetlejuice, Heathers, Edward
Scissorhands, and Reality Bites.

4
00:00:21,192 --> 00:00:26,455
Stranger Things later introduced her to a new
generation without losing that distinctive
intensity.

5
00:00:26,555 --> 00:00:31,051
Meg Ryan became one of the era's essential romantic
comedy stars.

6
00:00:31,151 --> 00:00:41,392
When Harry Met Sally and You've Got Mail showed how
a pause, a look, or a perfectly timed line can make
a love story feel personal.

7
00:00:41,492 --> 00:00:49,819
Johnny Depp built an early career around unusual
choices, from Edward Scissorhands to Ed Wood and
Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas.

8
00:00:49,919 --> 00:00:55,181
His portraits reflect an actor drawn to
transformation rather than a single predictable
type.

9
00:00:55,281 --> 00:01:00,260
Take a moment with these images and remember where
you first saw them.

10
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:08,951
The nineties also made room for stars who could
move between music, comedy, drama, and action.

11
00:01:09,051 --> 00:01:19,012
Will Smith went from The Fresh Prince of Bel Air to
Independence Day and Men in Black with an ease that
made every new role feel like an event.

12
00:01:19,112 --> 00:01:28,380
Halle Berry combined charisma with risk taking
performances, from romantic drama to Storm in the X
Men films and her Oscar winning work in Monster's
Ball.

13
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:36,706
Uma Thurman brought a cool, precise presence to
Pulp Fiction, then returned to action in Kill Bill
with a completely different kind of force.

14
00:01:36,806 --> 00:01:45,480
These six faces helped define a decade, but their
later portraits remind us that a cultural moment is
only one chapter of a long career.

15
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The close-up chapter begins. Look again at the portraits, the years, and the roles.

16
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:31,600
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?

17
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:59,600
Sources, narration, original music and editorial credits.
